### KillBill × Hyperswitch Prism plugin — full flow (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client)
#
# Run the requests top to bottom. After a create, copy the returned id from the Location
# header (or response body) into the @vars below, then continue. (VS Code REST Client users can
# instead reference named requests, e.g. {{createAccount.response.headers.Location}}.)
#
# Prereqs: a running KillBill with killbill-hyperswitch installed; a real connector sandbox key.

@kbUrl        = http://127.0.0.1:8080
# Basic base64("admin:password"); regenerate if you changed the RBAC user.
@rbac         = Basic YWRtaW46cGFzc3dvcmQ=
@apiKey       = hyperswitch-test
@apiSecret    = hyperswitch-test-secret
@createdBy    = test-harness
@plugin       = killbill-hyperswitch
@amount       = 10.00
@currency     = USD

# Fill these in from the responses as you go:
@accountId    = PASTE_ACCOUNT_ID
@paymentMethodId = PASTE_PAYMENT_METHOD_ID
@paymentId    = PASTE_PAYMENT_ID

### 1. Create tenant (RBAC only; 409 = already exists, reuse it)
POST {{kbUrl}}/1.0/kb/tenants
Authorization: {{rbac}}
X-Killbill-CreatedBy: {{createdBy}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "apiKey": "{{apiKey}}", "apiSecret": "{{apiSecret}}" }

### 2. Upload plugin config for the tenant  (edit the connector + creds)
POST {{kbUrl}}/1.0/kb/tenants/uploadPluginConfig/{{plugin}}
Authorization: {{rbac}}
X-Killbill-ApiKey: {{apiKey}}
X-Killbill-ApiSecret: {{apiSecret}}
X-Killbill-CreatedBy: {{createdBy}}
Content-Type: text/plain

org.killbill.billing.plugin.hyperswitch.connector=stripe
org.killbill.billing.plugin.hyperswitch.environment=SANDBOX
org.killbill.billing.plugin.hyperswitch.captureMethod=AUTOMATIC
org.killbill.billing.plugin.hyperswitch.stripe.apiKey=sk_test_REPLACE_ME

### 3. Create account  -> copy the Location id into @accountId
# @name createAccount
POST {{kbUrl}}/1.0/kb/accounts
Authorization: {{rbac}}
X-Killbill-ApiKey: {{apiKey}}
X-Killbill-ApiSecret: {{apiSecret}}
X-Killbill-CreatedBy: {{createdBy}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currency": "{{currency}}", "name": "Test Harness", "email": "harness@example.com" }

### 4. Add payment method (card)  -> copy the Location id into @paymentMethodId
POST {{kbUrl}}/1.0/kb/accounts/{{accountId}}/paymentMethods?isDefault=true
Authorization: {{rbac}}
X-Killbill-ApiKey: {{apiKey}}
X-Killbill-ApiSecret: {{apiSecret}}
X-Killbill-CreatedBy: {{createdBy}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pluginName": "{{plugin}}",
  "pluginInfo": { "properties": [
    { "key": "ccNumber", "value": "4242424242424242" },
    { "key": "ccExpirationMonth", "value": "12" },
    { "key": "ccExpirationYear", "value": "2030" },
    { "key": "ccVerificationValue", "value": "123" },
    { "key": "ccFirstName", "value": "John" },
    { "key": "ccLastName", "value": "Doe" }
  ] }
}

### 5. Purchase  -> copy paymentId from the response body into @paymentId
POST {{kbUrl}}/1.0/kb/accounts/{{accountId}}/payments?withPluginInfo=true
Authorization: {{rbac}}
X-Killbill-ApiKey: {{apiKey}}
X-Killbill-ApiSecret: {{apiSecret}}
X-Killbill-CreatedBy: {{createdBy}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "transactionType": "PURCHASE", "amount": {{amount}}, "currency": "{{currency}}", "paymentMethodId": "{{paymentMethodId}}" }

### 6. Get payment (with plugin info)
GET {{kbUrl}}/1.0/kb/payments/{{paymentId}}?withPluginInfo=true&withAttempts=true
Authorization: {{rbac}}
X-Killbill-ApiKey: {{apiKey}}
X-Killbill-ApiSecret: {{apiSecret}}

### 7. Refund
POST {{kbUrl}}/1.0/kb/payments/{{paymentId}}/refunds?withPluginInfo=true
Authorization: {{rbac}}
X-Killbill-ApiKey: {{apiKey}}
X-Killbill-ApiSecret: {{apiSecret}}
X-Killbill-CreatedBy: {{createdBy}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": {{amount}}, "currency": "{{currency}}" }

### 8. (Optional) Capture a prior AUTHORIZE   POST /payments/{id}
# { "amount": {{amount}}, "currency": "{{currency}}" }

### 8b. (Optional) Void a prior AUTHORIZE
DELETE {{kbUrl}}/1.0/kb/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: {{rbac}}
X-Killbill-ApiKey: {{apiKey}}
X-Killbill-ApiSecret: {{apiSecret}}
X-Killbill-CreatedBy: {{createdBy}}

### 9. Replay a connector webhook to the plugin servlet
# NOTE: without a valid connector signature this returns {"status":"rejected"} (source not verified) — expected.
POST {{kbUrl}}/plugins/{{plugin}}/webhook
X-Killbill-ApiKey: {{apiKey}}
X-Killbill-ApiSecret: {{apiSecret}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "evt_test_harness_001",
  "object": "event",
  "type": "payment_intent.succeeded",
  "data": { "object": { "id": "pi_test_harness_001", "object": "payment_intent", "amount": 1000, "currency": "usd", "status": "succeeded" } }
}
